Placeholder License — Not Yet Selected
=======================================

CapsuleOS is in pre-1.0 development and **has not yet been released
under an open-source license**.  Until a license file is added to
this directory:

* All rights are reserved by the maintainer (TinchyChin,
  <tinchychin97@gmail.com>).
* No permission is granted to copy, modify, redistribute, or use the
  software for commercial purposes, derivative works, or any other
  purpose, express or implied, except with the maintainer's prior
  written consent.
* The "absence of a license" is **not** a permissive grant — the
  project defaults to the most restrictive interpretation under
  applicable copyright law (e.g. the Berne Convention, US 17 U.S.C.
  § 106A for derivative works).

Planned selection
-----------------
The maintainer intends to release CapsuleOS under one of the
following licenses, in priority order:

1. **Apache License 2.0** — explicit patent grant from contributors,
   patent retaliation clause, clear notice requirements.  Preferred
   for projects that may attract corporate contributors or users
   who care about patent safety.
2. **MIT** — short, permissive, no patent grant.  Preferred for
   maximum ecosystem compatibility and lowest friction.
3. **BSD 3-Clause** — similar to MIT, adds an explicit "no
   endorsement" clause.

This file is intentionally a placeholder so that:

  * downstream users and packagers do not mistake the project for
    being MIT/Apache/BSD licensed by default, and
  * the maintainer can swap in a real license text (e.g. the
    canonical Apache-2.0 from
    <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt>) in a single
    commit once a decision is made.

